<article class="env-remark" id="0FE4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FE4">Remark <span data-tag="0FE4">42.42.2</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$ satisfying the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0FE3" data-tag="0FE3">42.42.1</a>. Let $X = \coprod X_ n$ be the decomposition into open and closed subschemes such that every irreducible component of $X_ n$ has $\delta $-dimension $n$. In this situation we sometimes set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [X] = \sum \nolimits _ n [X_ n]_ n \in \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits ^0(X)  \]
</div>
  <p> This class is a kind of “fundamental class” of $X$ in Chow theory. </p>
</article>